<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <title>HTML QUOTATION</title>
    <style>
      #Quotation {
        padding-left: 100px;
        padding-right: 100px;
        color: rgb(97, 21, 21);
        font-size: 22px;
        text-align: center;
      }
      div {
        margin: auto;
        padding-left: 15px;
        padding-right: 15px;
        background-color: rgba(192, 152, 100, 0.794);
      }
      abbr {
        text-decoration: none;
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body style="background-color: rgb(228, 190, 95)">
    <h2 style="text-align: center"><u>QUOTATION</u></h2>
    <div style="border: 2px solid rgb(161, 55, 12); width: 500px">
      <span id="Quotation"><b>HTML QUOTATION TAGS EXAMPLE</b></span>
      <p><b>Address Tag</b></p>
      <blockquote>
        <address>
          123,House<br />
          Hill , New Road<br />
          HTML<br />
          <b>Contact US</b><br />
          Contact No:
          <a href="tel:1234567890">1234567890</a><br />
          EmailID:
          <a href="mailto: karljohn298@gmail.com">karljohn298@gmail.com</a>
        </address>
      </blockquote>
      <p>
        <cite
          ><q>Actions speak louder than words</q> | Let your words teach and
          your actions speak</cite
        >
        :- instead of just talking about doing something, it's more meaningful
        if a person actually does something. <br /><br />Written by
        <i>Abraham Lincoln</i>
      </p>

      <p><b>Abbreviation Tag</b></p>

      <p>
        The Phrase was 1<sup>st</sup> used in the form we use today in the
        <abbr title="United States">US</abbr> written by
        <abbr title="Abraham Linclon">A.L.</abbr>
      </p>

      <p><b>Always feel motivated!</b></p>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
